{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.ContentGenfunPalindromic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.ContentGenfunPalindromic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Units.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ContentGenfun.C4_first_moment_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ContentGenfun.C4_first_moment_zero","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/content-genfun-palindromic.lean#L63-L66","doc":"**First moment vanishes (n = 4 instance)**: `Σ_λ f^λ · content(λ) = 0` — the\nbar-even `O((q−1)²)` rigidity coefficient's linear term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ContentGenfun.C4_palindromic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ContentGenfun.C4_palindromic","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/content-genfun-palindromic.lean#L54-L61","doc":"**Palindromy (n = 4 instance)**: `C_4(q) = C_4(q⁻¹)`. Over the unit group the\nexponent flip `q ^ e ↦ q ^ (-e)` permutes the five terms, so no non-vanishing\nhypothesis is needed. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:content-genfun-palindromic","label":"prop:content-genfun-palindromic","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/content-genfun-palindromic.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ContentGenfun.C4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ContentGenfun.C4","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/content-genfun-palindromic.lean#L49-L52","doc":"`C_4(q) = q⁶ + 3q² + 2 + 3q⁻² + q⁻⁶` (the `n = 4` content generating\nfunction), read into `R` through the unit coercion. ","signatureChunk":0}]}